 Interview Prep: Common Commands Every DevOps Engineer Must Know

In most DevOps / Cloud interviews, you’re not rejected for tools —
you’re rejected because you can’t explain basic commands clearly.

Here are command categories interviewers expect you to know 👇

🔹 Linux (Daily Production Use)
ls, cd, df -h, du -sh, top, ps, kill, chmod, chown

🔹 Log Analysis & Debugging
tail -f, grep, awk, sed, less, journalctl

🔹 Networking & Connectivity
curl, ping, traceroute, netstat, ss, nslookup

🔹 Git (CI/CD Friendly)
git clone, git pull, git fetch, git rebase, git reset, git cherry-pick

🔹 Docker (Containers)
docker ps, docker logs, docker exec, docker build, docker inspect

🔹 Kubernetes (If You Claim K8s Experience)
kubectl get, kubectl describe, kubectl logs, kubectl exec, kubectl apply

💡 In interviews, they don’t ask commands.
They ask when, why, and what happens if it fails.

If you can explain real scenarios around these commands, you’re interview-ready.
